---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ProjectCard from '../components/ProjectCard.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Mechanical Design | SCT Engineering Works" description="High-precision mechanical design, special-purpose machines, CAD, GD&T, tolerance analysis, prototyping, validation, and production support." alternatePath="/fr/conception-mecanique/">
  <header class="container page-hero">
    <p class="section-kicker">Capability track 02</p>
    <h1>Mechanical design</h1>
    <p class="page-lede">I develop high-precision mechanisms and special-purpose equipment from functional requirements through architecture, CAD, tolerancing, prototyping, verification, and production handover.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="section container" data-reveal>
    <div class="capability-grid">
      <article class="capability-panel"><h3>Concept and architecture</h3><p>Decompose functions, compare concepts, define interfaces, select principles, and make key geometric and performance assumptions explicit.</p></article>
      <article class="capability-panel"><h3>Detailed design</h3><p>Develop assemblies and manufacturing drawings using SolidWorks, CATIA V5, AutoCAD, GD&T, tolerance analysis, and configuration discipline.</p></article>
      <article class="capability-panel"><h3>Analysis and risk control</h3><p>Apply kinematics, tolerance reasoning, SolidWorks Simulation, design reviews, and practical risk mitigation to precision systems.</p></article>
      <article class="capability-panel"><h3>Build and transfer</h3><p>Support prototyping, suppliers, DFM and DFA, testing, issue resolution, commissioning, documentation, and production handover.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section container" data-reveal>
    <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="section-kicker">Technical toolset</span><h2>Tools selected around the decision.</h2></div><p>Software supports the work; it does not replace clear requirements, sound mechanics, tolerance ownership, or physical validation.</p></div>
    <table class="evidence-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Area</th><th>Tools and practices</th><th>Typical deliverables</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>CAD and definition</strong></td><td>SolidWorks CSWP and Advanced, CATIA V5, AutoCAD, GD&T ASME Y14.5</td><td>Assemblies, detail drawings, tolerance schemes, design reviews</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Analysis</strong></td><td>Tolerance analysis, kinematics, SolidWorks Simulation, MATLAB</td><td>Trade studies, calculation notes, risk controls, verification targets</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Industrialization</strong></td><td>DFM and DFA, rapid prototyping, supplier coordination, BOM and configuration</td><td>Prototype builds, released packages, test hardware, handover documentation</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section class="section light-section" data-reveal><div class="container"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="section-kicker">Relevant work</span><h2>Mechanical design case studies.</h2></div><p>Examples span requirements-led artifact design, automated optical equipment, physical calibration references, and ultra-precision measurement machinery.</p></div><div class="project-grid">
    <ProjectCard eyebrow="Axiomatic design" title="Additive-manufacturing test artifact" description="Thirteen functional requirements and five constraints translated into fourteen measurable feature groups." href="/projects/axiomatic-am-test-artifact/" result="73.8 × 68.85 × 16.65 mm" featured />
    <ProjectCard eyebrow="Test systems" title="Automated optical test bench" description="Mechanical architecture developed for repeatability, access, calibration, and test execution." href="/projects/optical-test-bench/" result="±5 µm accuracy" />
    <ProjectCard eyebrow="Calibration hardware" title="3D optical calibration reference" description="A physical calibration artefact industrialized for repeatable use in production." href="/projects/3d-calibration-reference/" result="2 production sites" />
  </div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
